      "section": "origin",
      "body": "I am a mechatronics engineer and computer scientist. For eight-plus years, I have worked on AI and infrastructure, turning frontier research into products that ship, sell and get used. I was founder and CEO of Lilypad, a decentralised GPU network for verifiable AI inference across thousands of nodes, open-sourced when I led its wind-down in 2025 and arXiv-published. My previous roles include developer relations and go-to-market at IBM and the Filecoin Foundation, and technical architecture at Accenture.",
